{
  "description": "RuvNet Brain lifecycle hooks for Codex. Every command enters through a generation-independent wrapper and adapts the shared Brain hook bodies to Codex contracts.\n\nSCHEMA WARNING, MEASURED 2026-08-14 ON A LIVE CODEX 0.147.0 SESSION: this file accepts EXACTLY two top-level keys, `description` and `hooks`. Anything else and Codex logs `warning: failed to parse hooks config ...: unknown field `X`, expected `description` or `hooks`` and DROPS THE WHOLE FILE — all 16 hooks silently stop, on a warning line nobody reads. A structured `hostParity` object was written here first and did exactly that; the record below lives in this string because this string is the only place it can live.\n\nHOST PARITY (ADR-067). PreToolUse refusal routes through decision-gate.mjs on BOTH hosts, so decision-gate.mjs REFUSAL_POLICIES is the single list of policies and neither host can gain or lose one silently. This file deliberately does NOT restate that list: it used to name policies one by one, which is exactly why identifier-preflight, degradation-watch and adr-currency (added 2026-08-13) went live on Claude Code and were unreachable on Codex — a new policy had to be remembered twice, and nothing failed when it was not.\n\nDECLARED ABSENT — swarm-slot-recycler (Claude Code event TeammateIdle). Codex 0.147.0 has no TeammateIdle hook event. Its complete event set, read from the binary rather than assumed, is pre_tool_use, permission_request, post_tool_use, pre_compact, post_compact, session_start, session_end, user_prompt_submit, subagent_start, subagent_stop, stop. There is nothing to register against.\n\nOUTPUT CONTRACT. PreToolUse/PostToolUse/SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit stdout is PARSED by Codex (\"hook returned invalid post-tool-use JSON output\"); SessionEnd has no output schema at all and PreCompact carries no additionalContext. codex-hook-adapter.mjs enforces this per event.\n\nSESSIONEND IS HARD-CAPPED AT 3s BY THE HOST, measured on a live Codex 0.147.0 session which says so itself: `warning: clamping SessionEnd hook timeout to 3s`. A larger number here is not a longer budget, it is a lie the host silently corrects. learn-flush needs 18s (measured 18342/18347/18384 ms with a real queue and real ruflo), so codex-hook-wrapper.mjs DETACHES it: the cap governs how long the host WAITS, not how long work may take.",
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact|fork",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node -e \"const f=require('node:fs'),o=require('node:os'),p=require('node:path'),c=require('node:child_process'),d=process.env.CODEX_HOME||p.join(o.homedir(),'.codex'),b=process.env.RUVNET_BRAIN_HOME||p.join(p.dirname(d),'.cache','ruvnet-brain'),w=p.join(b,'codex-hook.mjs');let s;try{s=f.statSync(w)}catch{}if(!s?.isFile())process.exit(0);const r=c.spawnSync(process.execPath,[w,...process.argv.slice(2)],{stdio:['inherit','pipe','pipe'],encoding:'utf8',env:process.env,timeout:Number(process.argv[1]),killSignal:'SIGKILL'});if(r.status===0||r.status===2){if(r.stdout)process.stdout.write(r.stdout);if(r.stderr)process.stderr.write(r.stderr)}process.exit(r.status===2?2:0)\" 4500 session-start",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [
